# lmlinux-ai-core — the ai-core file set, split per component.
#
# This file is rendered by build-deb.sh (the version placeholder below becomes
# the full Debian version); control.in stays a template so the version lives
# in one place.
#
# Runtime dependencies cover the NEEDED entries and symbol versions across all
# 62 files in the bundled llama.cpp b12669 tree (readelf -d/--version-info):
# - libc.so.6, libm.so.6 and ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 require at most GLIBC_2.34.
# - libgcc_s.so.1 requires at most GCC_3.4; every libgcc-s1 release satisfies it.
# - libgomp.so.1 requires at most GOMP_4.5 (introduced in GCC 6).
# - libssl.so.3 and libcrypto.so.3 (NEEDED by libllama-common.so and the
#   server implementation) require OPENSSL_3.0.0. Debian 13's libssl3t64 ships
#   both libraries and Provides libssl3; there is no separate libcrypto3 deb.
# - libstdc++.so.6 requires at most GLIBCXX_3.4.30 (GCC 12) and CXXABI_1.3.13.
# The libggml/libllama/libmtmd NEEDED entries are bundled sibling libraries,
# resolved through the engine's LD_LIBRARY_PATH, not additional system debs.
Package: lmlinux-ai-core
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: lmlinux project <lmlinux@localhost>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.13~), python3 (<< 3.14~), mount, libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1, libgomp1 (>= 6), libssl3t64 (>= 3.0.0), libstdc++6 (>= 12)
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: lmlinux local AI inference core (llama-server + hax)
 The lmlinux ai-core as a Debian package: official llama-server b12669 and
 hax 0.7.0, the persistent inference and model-import systemd units, and the
 unified `ai` entry point. Qwen3.5-4B GGUF is the default model payload.
 .
 The bundled /opt/ai-core/venv retains LiteRT-LM 0.19.2 as the non-default
 Gemma-flavor engine. The model payload is NOT part of this package: it is
 imported from installation media by ai-core-model-import.service (model as
 firmware).
